# Build-context exclusions for the CMS image.
#
# Dockerfile.prod does `COPY site /var/www/html/site`, which reads from the
# host filesystem and ignores .gitignore. Without this file, local build
# artifacts get baked into the image and into the kirby_data volume.
#
# IMPORTANT: do NOT exclude `vendor/`. The kirby-seo plugin ships its own
# PSR-4 autoloader (vendor/composer/autoload_psr4.php) for the tobimori\Seo\
# namespace — not just for Spatie. Excluding it breaks every page render that
# calls $page->metadata().

# Panel build toolchain for kirby-seo (~85 MB). The compiled assets
# (index.js / index.css) are committed, so this is never needed at runtime.
**/node_modules

# ...sauf puppeteer, dont Browsershot a besoin AU RUNTIME : browser.cjs fait
# `require('puppeteer')` depuis vendor/spatie/browsershot/bin/ et remonte
# jusqu'à ce node_modules. Sans lui, la génération des PDF casse en prod.
!site/plugins/kirby-foodlab/node_modules

# VCS + local dev tooling
.git
.gitignore
**/.husky
**/.php-cs-fixer.dist.php
**/.nvmrc

# Secrets are injected at runtime via compose `env_file`, never baked in
.env
